notes.body:
A PATCH request should change only the fields the client sent. That sounds simple, but C# makes it easy to get wrong: if the request class has a normal nullable property, a missing field and a field sent as `null` both arrive as `null`, and the server cannot tell "leave it alone" from "clear it".

NetTrello solves this by keeping each request field as a raw `JsonElement`. Its `ValueKind` tells three cases apart:

- `Undefined`: the field was not in the body, so keep the stored value;
- `Null`: the client sent `null`, so clear the field (if it is allowed to be empty);
- anything else: the client sent a value, which must be checked.

`ResolveAgainst(current)` does this for all six card fields at once and returns a complete set of values for the domain. The domain itself never sees JSON. Before you open the quizzes, read the trace lab section and the parser in `Contracts/BoardDtos.cs`.
